;; stdlib/redgarden/tree_passive_mod.prn — REDGARDEN's second real PARENA
;; mod, same minimal one-function/no-dispatch-table shape as
;; bloodflower_mod.prn (S194-01) and PITVIPER's vterm_mod.prn (S192-01).
;;
;; Founder real-time, 2026-08-25: "can you add a passive to tree that when
;; he is close enough to a tree to auto attack it he auto attacks it and
;; slowly regenerates health?" -> "the tree he attacks never does or
;; anything have it jiggle animate extra squishy" -> "as a parena first
;; mod led dev cycle" -- following the established "PARENA mod is the
;; trigger, host C does the real work" split bloodflower_mod.prn already
;; set, not inventing a new shape.
;;
;; "tree" here is the ARENA_HERO_TREE hero auto-attacking a nearby
;; ARENA_OBSTACLE_TREE jungle-decoration obstacle (packages/simulation/
;; arena_game.c's arena_obstacles_reset_layout) -- the existing decorative
;; trees that dot the map already had zero interaction; this is what gives
;; them HP, a hit reaction, and regen, gated to the one hero whose kit fits
;; the flavor.
;;
;; ABI: arena_hero_tree_passive (arena_game.c) calls straight into
;; `on-tree-passive-strike` (emitted as `on_tree_passive_strike`) once per
;; successful strike -- already gated by range/cooldown/hero-id checks on
;; the host side, this mod is never called for any other hero or out of
;; range. Calls back out to a host-provided
;; `redgarden_host_tree_passive_strike(hero_index, obstacle_index)` C
;; function (arena_game.c-side) to apply the real damage/heal/hit-reaction
;; trigger. Same #target/inline-c FFI-escape pattern editor/plugin.prn
;; (S189-29), vterm_mod.prn (S192-01), and bloodflower_mod.prn (S194-01)
;; all already established.

(module redgarden/tree-passive-mod)
(export on-tree-passive-strike)

(defn on-tree-passive-strike [(hero-index : I32) (obstacle-index : I32)] : Unit
  #target
  {:c (inline-c "redgarden_host_tree_passive_strike(hero_index, obstacle_index);")})
